.TH BIOKIDS\-SHELL 1 2026\-09\-30 "biokids 0.1.0" "BioKids"
.SH NAME
biokids\-shell \- the BioKids child launcher
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B biokids\-shell
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR port ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-kiosk ]
.RB [ \-\-log\-level
.IR level ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B biokids\-shell
is the full\-screen launcher a child sees after logging in: the applications
a parent allowed, and the time left today.
It runs in the child's own session as the systemd user unit
.BR biokids\-shell.service ,
serves the launcher on
.I http://127.0.0.1:7879/
by default, and shows it in a Chromium kiosk window.
The child's session starts it; it is not started by hand.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
Read the configuration from
.I file
instead of
.IR /etc/biokids/config.toml .
.TP
.BI \-\-port " port"
Override the port.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-kiosk
Serve the launcher without starting a browser.
For development only.
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-level " level"
One of debug, info, warning or error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR biokids\-voice (1),
.BR biokids\-daemon (8)
